<title>AUSTRALIA: Dominion Bridge cuts McConnell stake.</title>
<headline>Dominion Bridge cuts McConnell stake.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dominion Bridge Corp of Canada said on Wednesday it had cut its stake in Australian construction group McConnell Dowell Corp Ltd to 63.03 percent from 77.42 percent.</p>
<p>Dominion, formerly Cedar Group Inc, said earlier this month that it planned to cut its McConnell stake through the issue of six million shares to institutions.</p>
<p>The Canadian construction group acquired control of McConnell through a A$1.60 per share takeover offer last year.</p>
<p>At 11.40 a.m. (0040 GMT), McConnell shares were steady at A$2.25 in light volume.  </p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
